n Aug  7 09:25:28 1995  Mike Warren  <msw@sampson.145>

	* remesh.c: Rewrite to use memory more efficiently and to
	work in parallel.  I put most of the code that was remesh
	related in main_vrtx.c here as well.

	* GNUmakefile: Somebody has gratuitously screwed up the Makefile.
	I'm changing it to something that works for now.

Tue Aug  1 13:51:03 EDT 1995  Mike Warren
	
	* main_vrtx.c: Put the remeshing section back in.  There should
	be no change in behavior if remesh_freq == 0.

 	* main_vrtx.c: Do not decrement iter for RK steps.  The remesh_freq
	counter can not tell that an iteration has been done otherwise.
	I think iter should count force updates, not integrator steps.

	* main_vrtx.c: Don't keep remeshed particles that have strength
	smaller than the input parameter remesh_min_str.  I think the
	problems we were having were from particles that were incredibly
	weak.

